 // Register pressure under native widths.
@@ -158,19 +181,32 @@ MOSRegisterInfo::MOSRegisterInfo(const MOSSubtarget &STI,
 // that contains it count toward the same set, so the heuristics see that an
 // 8-bit value live across a 16-bit one competes for the same physical
 // register. That saves code size but costs cycles, so -O3 leaves it out.
+//
+// Without native widths, one set is appended instead: the accumulator, with
+// a limit of 1, because the 8-bit accumulator holds one value. The generated
+// sets count A only in GPR_LSB, together with X, Y and the flags, so without
+// it the pressure heuristics cannot see that a second live accumulator value
+// has to be copied out. MachineLICM then hoists values into A across loops,
+// and the scheduler lets accumulator values overlap. The MOS scheduler's
+// computed-carry model (MOSSchedStrategy) is tuned together with this set:
+// keeping accumulator pressure low interleaves multi-byte arithmetic, and
+// the carry model keeps the computed carries of those chains from
+// overlapping.
 bool MOSRegisterInfo::hasNativePressureSets() const { return STI.hasAccum16(); }
 
